      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the length of the tunnel. Let's break down the information given and use it step by step.\n\n1. **Determine the speed of the train in miles per minute:**\n   The train is moving at a speed of 60 miles per hour. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we convert the speed to miles per minute:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Speed} = \\frac{60 \\text{ miles per hour}}{60 \\text{ minutes per hour}} = 1 \\text{ mile per minute}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the distance the train travels in the time it takes to exit the tunnel:**\n   The train exits the tunnel 3 minutes after the front of the train enters it. Since the train travels at a speed of 1 mile per minute, in 3 minutes it will travel:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance traveled} = 1 \\text{ mile per minute} \\times 3 \\text{ minutes} = 3 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n   This distance of 3 miles is the total distance the front of the train travels to exit the tunnel, which is the length of the tunnel plus the length of the train.\n\n3. **Set up the equation to find the length of the tunnel:**\n   The total distance the train travels to exit the tunnel is the sum of the length of the tunnel and the length of the train. Let \\( L \\) be the length of the tunnel. The length of the train is 1 mile. Therefore, the equation is:\n   \\[\n   L + 1 = 3\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solve for the length of the tunnel:**\n   Subtract 1 mile from both sides of the equation:\n   \\[\n   L = 3 - 1 = 2\n   \\]\n\nThus, the length of the tunnel is \\(\\boxed{2}\\) miles.",
